/// Synopsis: a light color (a luma of 70% or more: `secondary` and `secondary-light`, the `-lighter` and `-lightest` tones, `quaternary-light`) in a box, a callout, an exercise and an example. The badge of the box has dark blue text, and what takes the color of the box (bold, alert, highlight, chip, link, icon, markers, arrows, the numbers of the lists of an exercise or an example, the label and the icon of a bar callout, the text and the logo of the footer of an exercise) is in the dark tone of its family, `secondary-dark` for the yellow, or, out of the palette, in the color darkened by 40%. The `===` pill of a yellow box is dark yellow with white text, and an alert in it is dark blue, as the yellow does not read on the dark yellow. The border of an exercise and the rules of its footer, its bottom border, keep the color of the box. In a box or a callout the numbers of the lists stay blue (page 3). Pages 5 to 7: a yellow exercise with a `===` repeated after `---` (pages 5 and 6) and the answer in the dark tone (the dashed rule, and the word a little darker), and a light green example with its solution.
#import "../../common.typ": *
#show: setup
#include "body.typ"
